{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAFUUSGH2ndQV17VXR9X","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`--and` patterns now get the same path-separator error as the primary pattern. Before, something like `fd foo --and one/two` just returned nothing without saying why. `cargo test` passes, including two new tests.\n\n**What changed** (`src/main.rs`):\n- I moved the separator check into a helper, `pattern_contains_path_separator`. It flags `/` on every platform. On Windows it also flags `\\`, but only when the pattern is an existing directory.\n- `ensure_search_pattern_is_not_a_path` checks the primary pattern first, then each `--and` pattern. `--full-path` still turns the check off for all of them.\n- The error for an `--and` pattern has its own wording and only suggests `--full-path`. The primary pattern's message also suggests `fd . '<pattern>'`, which doesn't make sense for an `--and` pattern:\n  ```\n  [fd error]: The '--and' pattern 'one/two' contains a path-separation character and will not lead to any search results.\n\n  If you want your patterns to match the full file path, use '--full-path'.\n  ```\n\n**Tests** (`tests/tests.rs`): one test checks that a `/` in an `--and` pattern is rejected, whether or not it names a real directory. The other checks that `--full-path` allows it (skipped on Windows, like the existing equivalent).\n\nI also added a Bugfixes line to `CHANGELOG.md`. Clippy reports a redundant `&` in the `anyhow!` call for the primary-pattern message. That code was there before and clippy already reported 18 warnings without my change, so I left it. Nothing is committed yet."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":500,"cache_read_input_tokens":37571,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":500,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9f5c9e1a-0998-48c2-8782-3d238a14f7e5","uuid":"73c83da4-cc35-4ce4-a76c-c23048a9a9f3","timestamp":"2026-10-18T19:25:08.348Z","request_id":"req_011CgAFUUDcdHnWuFV2RsdFs"}
